{"kind":"report","text":"CHANGES REQUESTED on exact clean pushed head 35c8ed81c143b8409fb44d70e67a5474fc41ba96. I retired my earlier approval ec0e8ec5 before it was ratified; main still does not contain this head.\n\nArchitecture: the head still preserves the documented kernel/application boundary, compact checkpoint v3 wire schema, streamed verification behavior, and 256 MiB serialized-artifact ceiling. The required repair belongs in internal/kernel; update docs/reference/architecture.md only if it changes that contract.\n\nSecurity: the claimed construction-peak bound is incomplete. writeCompactCheckpointEvent allocates names := make([]string, 0, len(event.Attachments)) and sorts it. On appendBorrowedChunk the cache reserve contains retained chunks plus the precharged list node, but no per-attachment charge for the borrowed Event, so this history-proportional string-header array coexists with the borrowed source, gzip state, and bounded output without appearing in checkpointChunkWriter.reserve. The tail map estimate cannot cover this path and is documented as map-only. A sufficiently attachment-heavy event therefore crosses the claimed instantaneous construction model before the bounded writer can refuse it. Separately, the writer accepts attachment counts through uint32 max while readCompactCheckpointEvent rejects counts above 1\u003c\u003c20; ingress and audit can carry more than 1\u003c\u003c20 empty attachments because the payload ceiling charges bodies but not names/count. The current writer can therefore publish a checkpoint its own decoder refuses.\n\nRepair requirements: preflight and explicitly reserve the attachment-name sorting storage before it is allocated on both borrowed and owned encoding paths, keep that reservation live through the event write, and release it afterwards without weakening the existing output-growth, in-hand-entry, tail, or node accounting. Align the writer count ceiling with the decoder so no emitted checkpoint is self-unreadable;